<!-- Overhaul of item pools given by npc traders valeria/diana/manx/procurator
All military and military ship items now at procurator. Civilian ship items at Valeria. Remaining items mostly split between diana and manx
Removed all productivity and maintanence items of common and rare rareties because they're of limited use. Epic versions are still available. Option to add these back
Removed all "area" specialists because slight buffs like +1 fire safety to a specific production building's radius that is also in range of an officium simply isn't worth a slot
Overall half of common and rare civilian items removed, around a third of civilian epics removed
All ship and military items remain available -->



<!-- I have left the specialist lists I made from the original gamefiles for anyone who comes across this in future. Same with my reference notes below -->

<!-- personal reference notes: -->
<!-- npc rivals (dorian etc.) item trades are linked to the "any common", rare, epic legendary pools. These pools are quite limited  -->
<!-- npc traders and pirates have specific pools with more items than the "any pools" -->
<!-- There is some difference in the pirate pools e.g. caeso has 2 more epics than the latium any epic pool -->
<!-- for each region combine the any, any of that region, trader 1, trader 2 and pirate pools to get a mostly full list of specialists-->
<!-- I did notice some things still missing and some specialists in regions that didn't make sense -->
<!-- There are legendary specialists from defeating/conquering each rival and another separate pool from research that I have not included -->


